\"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e15cbe2e54d64cbe0d7021d3445688155aab07afdd426cf4536225feb4e6156e","event_uuid":"ba00b742-f817-4a07-b37a-f65ffc8b91fb","position":{"commit_sha":"25501307aa483a57745abb82fbae72dcc6bc2310","position":"1788077321698692001-ba00b742-f817-4a07-b37a-f65ffc8b91fb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"825b07d348fe1fc00118252e4e50fb88f078d9018961a0fdbf0ec5e245984f9b","event_uuid":"359a054e-b50f-47f5-9e07-8df4bd35b4ca","position":{"commit_sha":"e69b636bc2f837d2a987a29f7c69c5e8d0bda2ec","position":"1788077628362765001-359a054e-b50f-47f5-9e07-8df4bd35b4ca"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"34805accf27f52a1857b8a96f9eebf97cc38c09f41e64ef11fc9e8b32836dd2a","event_uuid":"c6cda154-ea65-48db-a25d-6e1db870b956","position":{"commit_sha":"a3bd444bab6b97d2b72f1c9545ffaae2da083f72","position":"1788077945825556001-c6cda154-ea65-48db-a25d-6e1db870b956"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5b5f0276cdf921f97974ec8b28cede67de80bdf0bdfc716935dd04fdc0f8f9e7","event_uuid":"c6ecbee2-dccd-4818-96ea-0a4d297f728d","position":{"commit_sha":"bfceaac4d69a1cbd476964098c7c0f7010eec61f","position":"1788077951978666001-c6ecbee2-dccd-4818-96ea-0a4d297f728d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Refined-bar reinforcement (stays READY-TO-FIX; sharpened recommendation)\n\nThe refined standard confirms this as the ROOT correction and clarifies the target code. **Do NOT split into several narrow codes.** The one honest principle for branch 6:\n\n- Keep `llm_unavailable` for `isinstance(exc, LLMUnavailableError)` (incl. LLMConfigError) — its scenario set (extra absent, credentials missing/invalid, provider unreachable/rate-limited/refused) accurately fits the name.\n- Everything else under `LLMError` → `command_failed`, the existing broad-but-accurate \"an unclassified rebar command failure.\" That code honestly covers the whole residual set (input rejections, tool-loop/budget self-stops, context-window, output defects, and — pending 73d8 — workflow/expression faults) WITHOUT naming a wrong cause.\n\n**Why `command_failed` and not new vocab:** per the 35ab/551b precedent, grow vocabulary only for demonstrated observable need. `command_failed` is not misleading for these scenarios — it makes no false cause claim — so it is an accurate fit, just broad. Finer per-type codes (input_rejected, output_invalid, …) are OPTIONAL and should be filed separately only if a consumer needs the distinction.\n\nImplementation note: narrowing branch 6 to `LLMUnavailableError` is the single change that also fixes 7d47 (load-time WorkflowError) and resolves the 73d8/551b tension (a genuine execute-time outage is an `LLMUnavailableError` and stays `llm_unavailable`; an `ExpressionError` is not, so it correctly falls to `command_failed`).","timestamp":1788056972582380283},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## DECISION RECORDED — Option B approved (operator)\n\nThe operator approved **Option B**: split the overloaded `coverage.llm_unavailable` boolean rather than widen it into a vague `degraded`. Operator rationale, verbatim intent: *\"'degraded' is exactly the kind of overly broad and easily misinterpreted category that causes LLMs problems interpreting the output.\"*\n\n**This ticket is now READY-TO-FIX (no longer an open escalation).** Concrete plan:\n1. In `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`, stop folding `LLMInputRejectedError` into the `llm_unavailable=True` arm. Keep `coverage.llm_unavailable=True` **only** for genuine availability faults (`LLMUnavailableError`/`LLMConfigError`).\n2. Add a distinct, accurately-named signal for input rejection — an `input_rejected` boolean (or equivalent) on the degraded verdict — set when the cause is `LLMInputRejectedError` (oversized/malformed prompt, content-policy refusal).\n3. Update the three consumers that branch on the boolean to read the correct signal: `plan_review/drift_floor.py:202`, `plan_review/orchestrator.py:468`, `review_bot/adapter.py:114`.\n4. Do NOT introduce a broad `degraded` category (explicitly rejected).\n\nCoordinate with f75f's `error_code_for` branch-6 narrowing (same unified principle: reserve `llm_unavailable` for real outages, route non-availability faults to accurately-named signals). Retag escalate → ready-to-fix.","timestamp":1788059880887247753},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented + pushed as **Gerrit 2418** (stacked on 2416/0aee → 2415/fbc0 → 2413/f75f).\n\nOption B (operator-approved) — split the overloaded `coverage.llm_unavailable`:\n- New helper `failure.degrade_cause_flags(error)` → mutually-exclusive `{llm_unavailable, input_rejected}`; `LLMInputRejectedError`→`input_rejected`; else (incl. string tail)→`llm_unavailable`.\n- Both degrade builders route through it (`_degraded_code_review_verdict`, `_degraded_plan_review_verdict`).\n- 3 readers honour it, degrading exactly as for an outage (never hollow PASS): `finalize_verdict`→INDETERMINATE; `drift_floor._recompute_verdict_after_drop` BLOCK→INDETERMINATE; `review_bot/adapter` distinct `input-rejected` gap reason kept OUT of `RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS` (honest fail-closed, not deferred retry). No broad `degraded` category.\n\nHeld-out TDD: happy-path oracle (helper + code-review builder) shown to implementer; edge/E2E/reader oracle (string default, plan-review E2E, all 3 readers) held out. RED-first 7 failed for right reason → implementer (happy-path only, 1 attempt) → restored full oracle 7 passed. sandbox-exec mutation-teeth: 4 perturbations each killed a held-out test, restored GREEN. lint+typecheck clean; C901 finalize_verdict=11 / _recompute=5. Targeted regression 153 passed. Close pending Verified+1 + LLM-Review+1 on 2418.","timestamp":1788071281622233672}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788056654204157913,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"42520c6f-6007-4f51-abe7-46bdd7bce37a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9bb3-9fd0-7cb2-4fc8"}],"description":"## Finding (audit of epic 3405-c0b7)\n**Site:** the gate degrade producers in `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` — `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (via the `except (LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` arm at line 203), `_degraded_code_review_verdict` (line ~336 sets `\"llm_unavailable\": True`), and the completion-verdict degrade. They emit `coverage.llm_unavailable = True`.\n\n**Problem:** the arm catches `(LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` together (comment at line 203 folds `LLMInputRejectedError`, bug 43d4, into \"the mid-run infra outage\" arm). So when the cause is an INPUT REJECTION (oversized/malformed prompt, content-policy refusal), the verdict still carries `coverage.llm_unavailable=True`. The field's docstring admits the name is overloaded to mean \"no provider record accompanies this verdict\" (degraded), NOT literally \"the provider is down\".\n\n**Wrong signal:** `coverage.llm_unavailable=True` for a non-availability fault. `resolution_fields(outcome)` DOES ride the truthful `resolution_class` (CHANGE_INPUT) alongside, so the disposition is recoverable — but the boolean's NAME misreports the cause.\n\n**Consumers that branch on the boolean:** `plan_review/drift_floor.py:202`, `plan_review/orchestrator.py:468`, `review_bot/adapter.py:114`.\n\n**Observable vs latent:** OBSERVABLE — on every degraded gate verdict JSON and to the three consumers above.\n\n**Proposed fix (needs decision):** behavior-change / rename — either split the flag (a neutral `degraded` / `no_provider_record` boolean vs a strict `llm_unavailable` reserved for real outages) or have consumers/readers key off `resolution_class` instead of the overloaded boolean. Affects the verdict contract and three consumers → **escalate**.\n\n**caused_by / class:** the same \"input-rejection framed as provider outage\" pattern; origin 8a31 / bug 43d4.\n\n## Operator decision (approved: Option B)\nSplit the overloaded `coverage.llm_unavailable` boolean: keep it True ONLY for genuine availability outages; add a distinct `input_rejected` signal for `LLMInputRejectedError`. Do NOT introduce a broad `degraded`/`no_provider_record` category (operator explicitly rejected it).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A single source-of-truth helper `degrade_cause_flags(error)` in `src/rebar/llm/failure.py` returns mutually-exclusive coverage flags — `input_rejected=True` for `LLMInputRejectedError`, else `llm_unavailable=True` (real outages and the string-error degrade tail).\n- [x] Both degrade builders emit the split signal through that helper: `_degraded_code_review_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`) and `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py`).\n- [x] The three readers honor the split: `plan_review/drift_floor.py` (veto branch), `plan_review/orchestrator.py` (maps `input_rejected` to INDETERMINATE), and `review_bot/adapter.py` (non-retryable `input-rejected` coverage-gap reason, deliberately NOT in `RETRYABLE_GAP_REASONS` — a deterministic input rejection is an honest fail-closed veto, not a deferred retry).\n- [x] `coverage.llm_unavailable` is no longer True for an input-rejection fault; the new `input_rejected` flag carries it instead, preserving real-outage behavior unchanged.\n- [x] A held-out oracle proves the split through the real surfaces (helper contract, string-error edge, plan-review E2E, all three readers); checked: `python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96.py tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96_heldout.py -q` passes.\n\n## Testing\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96.py tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96_heldout.py -q`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/failure.py","reason":"Add single-source degrade_cause_flags(error) helper returning mutually-exclusive {llm_unavailable,input_rejected}"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"Code-review degrade builder routes LLMInputRejectedError to input_rejected via the shared helper (llm_unavailable stays True only for real outages)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/plan_review_recovery.py","reason":"Plan-review degrade builder uses the same shared helper so both writers emit the split signal consistently"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/drift_floor.py","reason":"Reader: veto branch honors input_rejected alongside llm_unavailable"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py","reason":"Reader: finalize_verdict maps input_rejected to INDETERMINATE alongside llm_unavailable"},{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/adapter.py","reason":"Reader: add non-retryable input-rejected coverage-gap reason (honest fail-closed veto, not deferred retry)"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96.py","reason":"Happy-path oracle: helper contract + code-review builder"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_coverage_input_rejected_5f96_heldout.py","reason":"Held-out oracle: string-error edge, plan-review E2E, all 3 readers"},{"path":".gitignore","reason":"Ignore .git-msg/ dev-scratch dir used for commit-message files during this work"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","3405-c0b7-0436-4b46"],["relates_to","9bb3-9fd0-7cb2-4fc8"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3405-c0b7-0436-4b46","parent_status_uuid":"c6cda154-ea65-48db-a25d-6e1db870b956","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["error-taxonomy","observable","ready-to-fix"],"ticket_id":"5f96-25aa-af9d-4f57","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gate degrade sets coverage.llm_unavailable=True for LLMInputRejectedError (overloaded/misleading boolean)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3f5b2b0b-d9ea-4804-b79d-02ee4ae4c886","406cf018-374a-4f83-9d2f-dc954fcd7a76","6f6cb13f-8f5c-4c55-bd87-0d112505e9b6","b984494f-cf03-4c53-924f-0092855cd30b","389b726c-a221-4d03-a2e9-589103a4f3e9","948d25c3-a072-4118-ad3a-af5cd530ff90","42520c6f-6007-4f51-abe7-46bdd7bce37a","277e5b59-94a5-4eba-b382-2ad5c3d655c6","ba00b742-f817-4a07-b37a-f65ffc8b91fb","359a054e-b50f-47f5-9e07-8df4bd35b4ca","c6cda154-ea65-48db-a25d-6e1db870b956","c6ecbee2-dccd-4818-96ea-0a4d297f728d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788087224176683001,"uuid":"b3a79fdd-0b85-411f-9efb-939d4e60efca"}